From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:25:12 +0200
Subject: nv30: GL_POINT_SMOOTH points are round (NV30_POINT_SMOOTH)

Yamagi Quake II's gl1 renderer draws its particles (blood, sparks, bullet trails) as GL_POINTS
with GL_POINT_SMOOTH and ARB_point_parameters; on the PS3 they came out as squares (2026-10-26,
round on llvmpipe). nv30 ignored pipe_rasterizer_state::point_smooth: NV3x/NV4x have no known
point smoothing switch (nouveau's method list has none, nor has the RSX's libgcm), and the state
tracker leaves the smoothing to the driver (radeonsi and zink run nir_lower_point_smooth on a
fragment shader variant).

nv30 does the same on its TGSI: points drawn with point_smooth (the reduced primitive is points,
hardware TnL) run a variant of the bound fragment program, made at the first such draw
(nv30_point_smooth.c). It declares a PCOORD input, which nvfx puts in a free texture coordinate
with the point sprite's coordinate replacement (as for gl_PointCoord), and adds about 20
instruction slots: the distance from the centre, the size in pixels from 1 / |ddx(pc.x)|, the
fragment killed outside the circle, COLOR[0].a times the coverage of a one pixel edge,
clamp(r - d, 0, 1), as nir_lower_point_smooth. The application's blending does the rest.
- nv30->fragprog.user: the bound program; fragprog.program, what the GPU runs, is it or its
  variant (nv30_fragprog_select() before each draw). The blitter saves the bound one.
- nv30_validate_point_coord(): POINT_SPRITE_ENABLE for the variant.
- The variant's point coordinate slot counts as free for the vertex program (it routes nothing
  there either), so switching between the two keeps the vertex program's code.
- No variant (the points stay square): no COLOR[0] output, RET/CAL in the program, all ten
  texture coordinates in use, a translation failure.
- Deleting a program forgets it as the one the GPU holds (a later program at the same address
  is uploaded and bound).
NV30_POINT_SMOOTH=0: square points, as before.

Host test mesa/tests/point-smooth-test.c (tools/run-tests.sh mesa-point-smooth): the variant on
Mesa's TGSI interpreter over each point's square (sizes 1 to 64), its NV40 translation; PS3 check
ps3-gpu-tools/mesa-tests/gl-pointsmooth.

